# XMPL100 Driver

<p>A C++20 driver for the XMPL100 temperature switch, read through two GPIO pins of any MCU.</p>

[Quickstart](quickstart.md){ .md-button .md-button--primary }
[API guide](api-guide.md){ .md-button }
[Source on GitHub](https://github.com/kokeb-labs/driver-template){ .md-button }
</div>

The driver has no platform code and the part has no data bus. You give it a small class that reads one pin (and,
optionally, drives another); it does the rest: start-up timing, the self-test check and filtered readings.

